.TH LFS-POOL-PIN_INFO 1 2026-09-14 "Lustre" "Lustre User Utilities"
.SH NAME
lfs-pool-pin_info \- report OST pool pinning status
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY "lfs pool pin_info"
.B --pool
.IR POOL
.RB [ --quiet ]
.RB [ --file ]
.IR FILE " | " DIRECTORY " ..."
.SY "lfs pool pin_info"
.B --pool
.IR POOL
.RB [ --quiet ]
.B --fid
.IR MOUNT
.IR FID " ..."
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B lfs pool pin_info
subcommand queries the
.B lustre.pin
extended attribute of Lustre files and directories in order to report whether
they are pinned to a particular OST pool.  Pool pins are stored as YAML entries
of the form
.B pool:
.IR POOL
inside the
.B lustre.pin
attribute, alongside any other keys that may be present.
.PP
For each target specified on the command line,
.B lfs pool pin_info
checks whether its
.B lustre.pin
attribute currently contains a
.B pool
entry for the requested
.IR POOL .
The output consists of one line per argument in the form
.I "TARGET:POOL: pinned"
or
.I "TARGET:POOL: UNPINNED".
.PP
The
.B --fid
form of the command operates on files referenced by Lustre FIDs beneath the
filesystem mounted at
.IR MOUNT ,
while the default and
.B --file
forms operate on filesystem paths.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --pool " " POOL
Name of the OST pool whose pin status should be queried.  The name must
consist of only alphanumeric characters, underscores and hyphens, and may
optionally be qualified with an
.IR fsname
prefix (e.g.
.IR fsname . POOL ),
which is discarded before the pool name is used.
.TP
.BR -f ", " --file
Interpret remaining arguments as filesystem paths (this is the default if
neither
.B --file
nor
.B --fid
is given).
.TP
.BR -F ", " --fid " " MOUNT
Interpret remaining arguments as Lustre FIDs within the filesystem mounted at
.IR MOUNT .
This option is mutually exclusive with
.BR --file .
.TP
.BR -q ", " --quiet
Suppress both the per-target error messages (such as a target that cannot be
opened or an unrecognized FID) and the per-target
.IR "TARGET:POOL: pinned" " / " "TARGET:POOL: UNPINNED"
status lines; the exit status still reflects the pinning state and any errors
encountered.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Display brief usage information for the
.B lfs pool pin_info
subcommand.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The
.B lfs pool pin_info
command returns a status that reflects both the success of the query and the
pinning state of the targets:
.TP
.B 0
All specified targets were successfully queried and are pinned to the requested
.IR POOL .
.TP
.B 1
All specified targets were successfully queried but at least one target is not
pinned to the requested
.IR POOL .
.TP
.B > 1
An argument or lookup error occurred, such as an invalid pool name, an
unreachable filesystem, or a missing file or FID.  In these cases the exit
status is a positive errno value corresponding to the first error encountered.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check whether a file is pinned to pool scratch:
.EX
.B $ lfs pool pin_info --pool scratch /mnt/testfs/file
.EE
.PP
Check whether a file referenced by FID is pinned to pool scratch:
.EX
.B $ lfs pool pin_info --pool scratch --fid /mnt/testfs 0x200000401:0x1:0x0
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
The
.B lfs pool pin_info
command is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lfs (1),
.BR lfs-pool (1),
.BR lfs-pool-pin (1),
.BR lfs-pool-unpin (1),
.BR llapi_pool_is_pinned_file (3),
.BR lustre (7)
